<?php

namespace App\Services;

use App\Enums\PhaseKind;

/** Seven fixed contracts. Shared paragraphs are private text, not a capability framework. */
final class ParticipantPhaseInstructions
{
    // Relevant in phases 1–6; deliberately absent from terminal Order.
    private const EVIDENCE = <<<'PROMPT'
Existing local mutable Writes may expose instrument.execute and attestation.create only as authorized by the schema. Instrument records an observation subject and creates an immutable Proposition-grounded Receipt local to the observed Proposition’s Commit Region; it never automatically loads evidence or verifies truth. Variant and revision start fresh evidence; reclassification retains effective evidence and its exclusions. Equivalent direct or inherited evidence blocks a repeated Instrument invocation regardless of who loaded it; instrument_exclusions supplies the target restrictions. Variant children alone do not disqualify an Instrument target. Hyperlink observes the canonical public domain/path without query or fragment and applies server stability checks. Web Search discovers up to five resources from a non-empty query of at most 1000 characters. Creating a Cite Receipt does not itself grant Reinforcement. A Tragedy Receipt is a dedicated homologous boundary-exit warrant, not ordinary evidence. It may be loaded and unloaded as cognitive memory of the failed committed lineage, never as evidence or Reinforcement. It cannot be replayed and does not satisfy Instrument, Attestation or generic shared-evidence requirements. Catalogue visibility grants no such authority.
Instrument execution may perform a new Citation, Hyperlink or Web Search observation, or replay an eligible prior Receipt using instrument.replay_receipt_id. Replay restores the immutable stored invocation, follows the same target eligibility and evidence exclusions, and creates a new Receipt with provenance. It never modifies or automatically loads either Receipt. Optional receipt_options on a successful forward contribution changes the Participant’s loaded state for current Gate evidence references or available scoped Tragedy memory. Rest does not accept these options. Persistent ordinary evidence load state contributes participant-specific Reinforcement; Tragedy memory never does. Loading is independent of boundary authority and memory survives consumption or exhaustion until unloaded; full evidence appears only when its grounded Proposition occupies the current Read.
attestation.create requires support or refute in direction; optional rationale never replaces direction. Other actions accept no rationale. The schema binds direction choices to exact targets. Opposite-direction Attestation supersedes the personal judgment; same-direction re-attestation is unavailable. Spent Writes remain evidence without Traverse, Attestation or redundant Instrument targets. continuation_exhausted marks successful history whose actual continuation is exhausted, not new actionability or generation capacity. Another live causal continuation keeps a shared source live.
PROMPT;

    private const TRAVERSE = <<<'PROMPT'
proposition.traverse selects an authorized causal Write by proposition_id and advances the Phase without creating content. An effective personal Attestation from an earlier Cycle replaces that same direction with Traverse; the opposite direction remains available through Attestation supersession. Receipt consumption does not erase that established path when the route is not currently spent. Another Participant's Attestation, a matching register or a same-region Write does not create personal Traverse eligibility.
PROMPT;

    private const REVISION = <<<'PROMPT'
When proposition.revise is exposed, it targets the exact owned active local Write with effective self-Refute from an earlier Cycle, never the Gate or a different producing position. Revision starts fresh votes, touches and evidence; it never resets generation.
PROMPT;

    private const GENERATION = <<<'PROMPT'
Variant is shared structural opportunity, never a Participant quota or fixed sibling cap. An empty viable position can offer it; a viable existing route blocks redundant generation. Further Variant requires the position's existing routes to be spent in its current exploration epoch with the existing evidence prerequisites. Potential is descriptive and does not govern expressive actionability. Only a successful Variant advances its own Horizon/structural-position epoch. Historical failures remain evidence but cease excluding a route when its applicable epoch advances; other positions' epochs remain independent. Receipt creation or consumption and revision do not reopen generation.
PROMPT;

    private const RECLASSIFY = <<<'PROMPT'
proposition.reclassify takes proposition_id and receipt_id, preserves the exact source statement and creates one hard causal reclassify edge. It requires an effective source Attestation, a completed Receipt and the selected available same-Commit-Region Receipt under the schema's full prerequisites; Reinforcement is not a prerequisite. Non-Bias Reclassification always requires ordinary evidence and cannot consume a Tragedy Receipt. For Bias, local and recorded mediated sources require ordinary own-Region Receipts and reject Tragedy Receipts. Foreign homologous escape requires the exact current-Region unresolved Tragedy Receipt bound to that source by the schema; ordinary Receipts cannot authorize it. Attachment atomically consumes that shared Receipt once and retains it by reference. Votes and Phase touches start fresh; old Attestations are not copied. There is no second source or authored statement. Each source/destination classification is created once globally; existing local Writes keep their schema-authorized actions.
PROMPT;

    private const VARIANT_EVIDENCE = <<<'PROMPT'
Each new Variant needs its own completed Instrument and effective Attestation. A Write without its own completed Instrument can expose Instrument even if other shared evidence exists; its own Instrument plus available shared evidence unlocks Attestation. Further Variant requires every current route to meet those evidence prerequisites as well as current spentness. Zero Potential does not remove structural expression authority.
PROMPT;

    private const REST = <<<'PROMPT'
Rest ends the Cycle; the server derives rest_reason. Rest never creates Tragedy or Commit Region exhaustion, including no_remaining_potential Rest. The first fresh expressive result at zero canonical Charge records its governing Commit Region’s unique Tragedy and Receipt; the Region remains open. A later distinct fresh expressive zero-Charge result in that same open Region exhausts it, regardless of authorship or Receipt consumption. Positive-Charge expression remains ordinary even when Tension increases. Potential is descriptive and proves neither catastrophe nor exhaustion. Existing-proposition actions and recalculation do not create a new catastrophe. The Tragedy Receipt is a homologous boundary-exit warrant, not an exhaustion token. Successful escape alone does not exhaust the Region. Exhaustion removes its live warrant authority. Recovery does not move its scope into another Region; archived catalogue visibility does not supply foreign authority. Historical statements and proof identities remain unchanged.
Recovery stops at the nearest eligible non-exhausted Committal on the recorded backward lineage. A nearer unresolved basin blocks older ancestors regardless of Potential or Charge; attenuation remains in measurements, not destination selection. Each Committal governs its own Commit Region basin, including same-Horizon Commits. Exhausting that region permits recovery past it; exhausting the boundary-governing region permits crossing into its parent Horizon backward on that same lineage, never jumping to a Horizon opener or unrelated branch. No global scan proves Exhaustion. A viable destination prepares the next Cycle there; otherwise the current position is retained.
PROMPT;

    private const LATE_PHASE = <<<'PROMPT'
Dominance selects candidate inputs; admissibility governs Writes. Measurement population and actionable population are distinct, as are causal visibility and actionability. Component-direction agreement is coherence, not positivity: Positive/Positive and Negative/Negative both qualify, and numeric zero uses retained component directions. Admissibility constrains the transition, not its outcome or future descendants. No observable pole is preferred. Rest is available only when no admissible non-Rest action remains; Potential neither creates nor suppresses that authority. The schema is authoritative.
PROMPT;

    public function forPhase(PhaseKind $phase, bool $restAvailable = false): string
    {
        $contract = match ($phase) {
            PhaseKind::Distinguish => <<<'PROMPT'
The current Committal is the Gate. Write contains causally local distinctions in the Domain's Activity or Signal register, including legitimate same-position revisions. proposition.variant creates a structurally distinct continuation when authorized; it starts fresh votes, touches and evidence. Earlier alternatives can remain visible without being eligible actions.
PROMPT
                ."\n".self::GENERATION."\n".self::VARIANT_EVIDENCE."\n".self::TRAVERSE,
            PhaseKind::Persist => <<<'PROMPT'
Persist develops the selected distinction from its current causal Gate into the Domain's Frontier or Stance Write position. proposition.variant develops structure when authorized; existing causal Writes retain only their schema-authorized actions. A register label alone cannot supply producing-position identity or promote an unrelated Write. New expressive development starts fresh votes, touches and evidence.
PROMPT
                ."\n".self::GENERATION."\n".self::REVISION."\n".self::TRAVERSE,
            PhaseKind::Constrain => <<<'PROMPT'
The current Persist-produced Frontier/Stance source is being constrained into its causal Canon/Concord classification. Writes are local continuations of this Gate, including legitimate same-position revisions. Instrument observations and Attestations keep their own meanings; neither rewrites the source statement or substitutes for Receipt attachment.
PROMPT
                ."\n".self::RECLASSIFY."\n".self::REVISION."\n".self::TRAVERSE,
            PhaseKind::Disperse => <<<'PROMPT'
Disperse develops plurality from the current Constrain-produced Gate. Its Activity/Signal Writes are causal continuations of that constrained route, including legitimate same-position revisions. proposition.variant creates a structurally distinct continuation with fresh votes, touches and evidence when authorized. This position's exploration epoch is independent of the earlier distinction position; reopening one never reopens the other.
PROMPT
                ."\n".self::GENERATION."\n".self::VARIANT_EVIDENCE."\n".self::REVISION."\n".self::TRAVERSE,
            PhaseKind::Mediate => <<<'PROMPT'
The preceding Disperse path in this same Cycle supplies the authoritative Read anchor: that Disperse Phase's recorded Constrain-produced Gate, not the current Mediate Gate or a guessed ancestor. Missing history does not authorize inventing an anchor. read_options contains only that one causal Read anchor. The ordinary local Reconcile path retains its existing eligibility even when this Read opposes the population direction.
Internally, the full homologous Constrain Read population supplies independently lineage-derived Correspondence measurements, including the acting Read exactly once. Homology requires the same substrate, proposition Domain, canonical Phase/Register position, tier and full committed depth from the shared Origin; Regions and Horizons may differ. Dominant Correspondence across homologous Reads qualifies additional active Reads by their own direction, retaining their own prior direction at numeric zero. A zero population mean retains prior population direction when supplied, or uses the positive Correspondence default; matching Reads may still supply counterparts. These population Reads are calculation inputs only, never visible Read alternatives.
gate_options can expose the current Gate and additional canonical Disperse Gates that are active immediate children of dominant-matching Reads in each Read's own Region and Horizon. Only schema-authorized other_proposition_id values are reconciliation counterparts. They are operands, never Traverse targets or movement destinations; foreign operands do not supply Receipt catalogue access. Reconcile requires the current Gate and counterpart to have matching retained Shape Topology/Cardinal Position directions individually, and their resolved Correspondence directions must agree with each other. Positive/Positive and Negative/Negative are both coherent; zero retains its component direction. An incoherent current Gate remains visible but cannot Write. Homologous operands are filtered only after full Read-population dominance. Attestation lean does not filter counterparts. The result remains in the acting Cycle's Region and Horizon, with the acting Phase Gate as traversed provenance.
proposition.reconcile takes only other_proposition_id besides action. Reconcile(current Gate, counterpart) copies the current Gate statement exactly and creates a new causal result with explicit hard parent edges from both inputs; there is no authored synthesis. The result is measured normally and need not preserve operand direction or coherence. Votes, Receipts and Phase touches are not inherited. Each directed pair may be generated once across all Participants; the inverse remains distinct because dominance differs. Existing Written results can expose evidence and Attestation actions; no preference between authorized actions is implied. Hard supersession does not globally consume inputs for other directed pairs. A completed Reconcile opens a directed incoming doorway from its exact selected operand to this result. A later Bias Gate produced along that operand’s immediately preceding Mediate path may use the result under ordinary Bias evidence rules. This creates no reverse doorway, movement or Receipt scope. Mediate does not expose expressive Traverse, even after personal Attestation.
PROMPT,
            PhaseKind::Bias => <<<'PROMPT'
Every Bias Reclassify source must also have equal retained Orientation and Attestation Cadence directions. Positive/Positive and Negative/Negative both qualify; zero uses retained direction. This checks the existing source, never a prospective result. The causal Gate remains readable when incoherent; unusable optional sources are absent. There is no requirement to match the current Gate’s Chirality direction. Reclassification results are measured normally and need not preserve source direction or coherence.
The current causal Gate retains its ordinary local Bias eligibility independently of the homologous population direction. Its retained evidence direction must agree with its own causal ancestry aggregate, excluding its own votes and loads. Both reconciliation parent paths count once, stop at the governing Committal and exclude unrelated siblings. At zero, this local evidence history retains its previous nonzero direction, seeded by the governing Committal.
Separately, the full homologous Mediate Gate population supplies independently lineage-derived numeric Chirality measurements. Same substrate, proposition Domain, canonical Phase/Register position, tier and full committed depth are required; Regions and Horizons may differ. Resolve dominance over the full population, including component-inadmissible members, before filtering dominant-matching active Gates for component coherence and ordinary Reclassify authority. Numeric zero retains the nearest preceding nonzero direction of that same structural population, including changes caused by Cycle entry and Attestation acts or replacements. An unavailable population inherits corresponding preceding-Horizon history; only the absence of all population history uses Chirality's Positive primitive default. Never borrow the acting member's direction. Population comparison never rewrites a Proposition's measurements or grants an action by membership alone.
Recorded incoming mediation is separate from homology: the current Bias Gate’s immediately preceding Mediate Gate identifies the exact earlier Reconcile operand. That doorway’s result can be an additional ordinary Bias source, independently of homologous direction. Mediate itself grants no movement. Only schema-authorized source/Receipt pairs may be used. Reclassify still requires an effective source Attestation, available completed unconsumed Receipt, unused source/register classification and an available continuation. The Receipt catalogue belongs to the acting Cycle's immutable entry Region; a foreign source never imports its Receipt stock. The selected source and Receipt may come from different Regions or Horizons.
Reclassify copies the selected statement exactly and creates one hard causal edge from that selected source to a new classification in the acting Bias Phase, Horizon and entry accounting Region. That newly produced classification becomes the forward position; the old Cycle entry does not change. No extra edge from the old Phase Gate is invented. Homologous Gates are not visible Read or Traverse alternatives. Existing local causal Writes retain their ordinary Instrument, Attestation and Traverse rules; another Cycle's foreign-source result is not adopted as a local Write.
A frozen successful classification remains traversable only from the exact Gate whose existing causal continuation produced it, subject to the schema and ordinary traversal prerequisites. Same-region or same-Horizon classifications from another Gate are never Traverse targets. Successful-route continuity preserves an edge; it does not create one. The frozen source stays immutable. Bias Traverse reaches Order through that classification's existing causal edge.
PROMPT
                ."\n".self::RECLASSIFY."\n".self::TRAVERSE,
            PhaseKind::Order => <<<'PROMPT'
Order's selected/current Gate is the Bias-produced classification. Read contains local Mediate-position Stance/Frontier ancestry. Order exposes the causally local Bias-produced expressive Writes associated with that Gate, including legitimate same-position revisions, alongside their own eligible direct Committal continuations. A sibling classification sharing a parent is not local merely for that reason.
Closure, performed during Order — Write, evaluates a new Committal observation for each causally local expressive Write. The source's Closure is frozen at its own birth and is never recalculated. The commitment and per-source commitment_options expose the authoritative new-Committal preview: Committed Cardinal Position (equal-weight full-ancestry Committal Depth and Lateral Committal Position) and historical per-Domain CV Cadence, with retained committed_cardinal_position_direction and cadence_direction. Their directions must agree. Temporary expressive positions never reserve committed slots. A new Committal can observe a different interval and Closure than its source. Origin's interval is 1; later Cadence is 0 until both creating Domains have at least two interval samples. Birth intervals count all Cycles entered in the exact entry/Horizon basin, including unfinished Cycles. Missing durable birth history makes Commit unavailable rather than reinterpreting history with current population. Preview does not create a causal edge or change stored Closure. Local expressive Writes remain visible regardless of Commit admissibility. The persisted consistency guard remains authoritative.
proposition.commit is available only where that local Write satisfies its full Commitment prerequisites, including a completed Receipt, fresh effective Attestation on the classification and aligned Committed Cardinal Position/Cadence with hysteresis. Reinforcement counts qualifying evidence uptake; it never changes observable values or substitutes for grounding. proposition_id selects that authorized Write. Commit preserves its exact statement and Commit-only participation history by reference, creates an immutable snapshot and consumes the direct source once globally; later evidence cannot rewrite it.
Local Commit and direct Committal Traverse remain independently available under their ordinary rules, regardless of population direction. Separately, homologous existing Committals at the Order Write position may add proposition.traverse options: same substrate, creating Domain, canonical Phase/register, tier and full committed depth from a validated shared Origin. Different Horizons and Regions are permitted. Legitimate frozen Commits embody their creation-time admissibility; do not calculate new Closure to authorize their selection. Preserve compatibility for unresolved historical evidence. Frozen Committed Cardinal Position and Cadence directions must agree; disagreement contributes no resolved direction. Order aggregates these resolved directions and offers active matching Committals. A tied aggregate retains supplied prior population direction, otherwise uses Closure's negative default. This never changes a proposition's frozen measurements or local Commit admissibility, imports evidence, or creates causal edges. Only schema-authorized targets may be selected. Order remains terminal: only schema-authorized Commit or Committal Traverse is available, or exclusive Rest when neither remains. Order introduces no new Attestation, Instrument, Revision, Reclassification or Variant actions. All grounding and attestation happen before Order. A successful Commit does not prescribe descendants’ Closure, Correspondence, Chirality directions or Domain trajectory. Commit and Committal Traverse complete this Cycle at that exact Committal; the next Cycle starts there under its applicable Horizon, without relocation.
PROMPT,
        };

        return "Current Phase: {$phase->value} {$phase->name}\n".$contract
            .(in_array($phase, [PhaseKind::Mediate, PhaseKind::Bias, PhaseKind::Order], true) ? "\n".self::LATE_PHASE : '')
            .($phase !== PhaseKind::Order ? "\n".self::EVIDENCE : '')
            .($restAvailable ? "\n".self::REST : '');
    }

    /** Change any instruction, including a conditional paragraph, and reversion the family. */
    public function fingerprint(): string
    {
        return hash('sha256', json_encode(array_map(
            fn (PhaseKind $phase): string => $this->forPhase($phase, restAvailable: true),
            PhaseKind::cases(),
        ), JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR));
    }
}
